Chapter: CtorLiteralNarrow

 Regression guard for FabledTreasureMap entry 11: variant fields
 narrow-store at their declared width since ctor packing, so an
 out-of-range literal at construction would silently truncate
 (300 stored into a 0..255 field reads back 44). The ctor-argument
 lint rejects the literal with CDX2050, mirroring the record-field
 rule.

Section: Definitions

  Byteish =
   | MkByte (Integer between 0 and 255)

  use-byte : Byteish -> Integer
  use-byte (b) = when b
   is MkByte (v) -> v

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (use-byte (MkByte 300)))
  end
